---
/* MediaGuard — casual-copy deterrence for artwork and player media.

   Self-contained on purpose. Three of the six pages (index, music, download)
   write their own <html> instead of using BaseLayout, and do not import
   global.css — so anything wired only into the layout silently misses the
   homepage and the music page, which is where the art actually lives. Both
   halves ship inline here, and `is:inline` keeps them out of the bundler, so
   no page can end up with a chunk that happens to omit the guard.

   Drop <MediaGuard /> into any page. It is idempotent — including it twice is
   harmless.

   WHAT THIS DOES
   Removes the one-click routes to a local copy: right-click "Save image as",
   drag-to-desktop, and the iOS long-press save sheet.

   WHAT THIS CANNOT DO — and no web code can
   Stop a screenshot, or stop someone lifting the file from the network tab or
   the disk cache. Both happen below the page. If the browser rendered it, the
   visitor already has the bytes. This is a speed bump, not protection. What
   actually protects the work is publishing display resolution rather than
   masters (artwork is capped at 1600px for this reason) and watermarking.

   DELIBERATELY NOT DONE
   Sitewide text-selection blocking and devtools/keyboard traps. Both are
   bypassed in seconds, both break accessibility and ordinary browser
   behaviour, and they make the site hostile to the collectors it exists to
   invite in. Please don't add them without re-reading this.
*/
---
<style is:global>
  img,
  picture,
  canvas,
  video,
  #lb-img,
  [data-artwork] {
    -webkit-user-drag: none;
    user-drag: none;
    -webkit-touch-callout: none;
    -webkit-user-select: none;
    user-select: none;
  }
</style>

<script is:inline>
  (function () {
    if (window.__dashMediaGuard) return;
    window.__dashMediaGuard = true;
    /* Delegated: the lightbox image is created after load. */
    var SEL = 'img, picture, canvas, video, audio, [data-artwork], #lb-img';
    var guarded = function (t) {
      return t && t.closest && t.closest(SEL) !== null;
    };
    document.addEventListener('contextmenu', function (e) {
      if (guarded(e.target)) e.preventDefault();
    });
    document.addEventListener('dragstart', function (e) {
      if (guarded(e.target)) e.preventDefault();
    });
  })();
</script>
